# Local package caches.
#
# Why this exists: this project runs inside a DSH file sandbox where writes are confined to
# the session workspace. npm defaults its cache to %LOCALAPPDATA%\npm-cache, which is outside
# it, so `npm install` fails with EPERM before it can unpack anything. A project-local cache
# keeps every write inside the sandbox.
#
# The Electron binary is a separate problem and is NOT solved here. npm 12 blocks install
# scripts by default, and this sandbox additionally forbids spawning a child process with
# piped stdio, which is how npm runs install scripts at all — so electron's postinstall
# cannot run here under any configuration. It must not be approved either: approving it makes
# npm attempt the spawn, and the install dies with EPERM. The binary is fetched explicitly:
#
#   npm install
#   npm run fetch:electron
cache=.npm-cache
